  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Jonah Heim's sac fly broke a tie in the tenth, but Arizona answered with two runs before the Athletics could blink.",
    "what_this_means": "Jacob Wilson carried the offense with a homer and two RBIs, and the lineup got runners on base. Converting three of seven RISP situations into runs. That should have been enough. Instead, the bullpen got into the game in the sixth, and while Brady Basso, Jos\u00e9 Suarez, Elvis Alvarado, and Hogan Harris kept things clean through eight, Luis Medina couldn't hold in the tenth when it mattered most. The Athletics trailed after one, fought back to tie it in the ninth, got the lead in the tenth. And lost anyway. Close games are becoming harder to win when you need the bullpen to finish them without a margin for error.",
